# Atlas Program KB

## Goals

### EU Launch
target: 2026-09-15

## Decisions

### Choose Stripe as payment provider
status: accepted
date: 2026-05-10
cites: PCI Compliance Audit 2026

Lower fees and stronger EU coverage than the incumbent.

### Use event sourcing for the billing ledger
status: accepted
date: 2026-05-22
cites: Latency Report Q2

Append-only ledger simplifies audit and replay.

### Deprecate the legacy REST API
status: proposed
date: 2026-06-03
cites: User Research June

Interviewees rely on the new endpoints already.

### Ship the EU region first
status: accepted
date: 2026-06-11
cites: User Research June

Largest waitlisted cohort is in the EU.

### Adopt Postgres 16 for the ledger store
status: superseded
date: 2026-04-18
cites: Latency Report Q2

Superseded by the event sourcing decision.

## Open Questions

### Do we need SOC2 certification before launch?
status: open

Until answered this blocks Run the penetration test.

### Can the exporter reuse the ledger schema?
status: open

Until answered this blocks Build the invoice PDF exporter.

### Is the latency budget 200ms or 300ms?
status: resolved

### Who signs the Stripe contract?
status: open

Until answered this blocks Integrate the Stripe checkout flow.

